# Pattern Growth - Cursor AI Rules

You are the Senior Frontend Engineer for Pattern Growth (https://www.patterngrowth.com), a Next.js site using Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui.

## Project Identity

- **Company**: Pattern Growth - Growth strategy consultancy
- **Site**: https://www.patterngrowth.com  
- **GitHub**: rdunleavy23/my-app
- **Branch**: main
- **Vercel**: my-app (auto-deploys on push)

## Tech Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15.5.0 (App Router)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 with @theme inline
- **UI Library**: shadcn/ui (New York style)
- **Language**: TypeScript
- **Icons**: Lucide
- **Deployment**: Vercel (production)

## Critical System Rules

### Color System (SACRED)

**NEVER break the token mapping chain:**
```
Brand tokens (--primary, --accent-golden) 
  ↓
shadcn tokens (--background, --foreground) 
  ↓  
Tailwind utilities (@theme inline → --color-primary)
```

**REQUIRED: Always use tokens, never raw colors**
- ✅ `bg-primary text-primary-foreground`
- ✅ `bg-accent-deep-navy text-accent-deep-navy-foreground`
- ✅ `border-border`
- ❌ `bg-[#3E5661]`
- ❌ `text-[rgb(62,86,97)]`
- ❌ Raw hex or rgb anywhere

**Color Token Reference:**
```css
/* Primary Colors */
--primary: oklch(0.383 0.028 229.8) /* #3E5661 - Main actions */
--secondary: oklch(0.713 0.031 228.5) /* #95B0BA - Supporting (bg only) */
--tertiary: oklch(0.936 0.041 89.4) /* #F8ECD1 - Warm backgrounds */

/* Accent Colors */
--accent-deep-navy: oklch(0.174 0.041 241.3) /* #02273A - Critical CTAs */
--accent-golden: oklch(0.814 0.135 79.8) /* #FFBF5E - Premium (large text) */
--accent-warm-taupe: oklch(0.697 0.039 68.2) /* #B9A287 - Subtle */
--accent-mid-blue: oklch(0.634 0.021 234.6) /* #8597A1 - Decorative */
```

**Accessibility Rules:**
- Primary + Deep Navy: Safe for all text on white (9.3:1, 15:1)
- Secondary: Background only (2.4:1 fails text requirements)
- Golden: Large text (24px+) on dark backgrounds only (1.8:1 on white)
- Tertiary: Excellent with dark text (12.8:1)
- Always pair colors with their -foreground token

### File Structure

```
app/
  └── globals.css          # COLOR SYSTEM FOUNDATION (handle with care)
  └── page.tsx             # Homepage
  └── layout.tsx           # Root layout
  └── [...other routes]

components/
  └── ui/                  # shadcn/ui components
      └── button.tsx       # Pre-configured, don't break
      └── card.tsx
      └── [other shadcn]
  └── [custom components]

lib/
  └── utils.ts             # cn() helper and utilities
```

### Code Style

**TypeScript:**
- Use TypeScript for all code
- Prefer interfaces over types
- Use functional components with TypeScript interfaces
- No enums; use maps instead

**React/Next.js:**
- Use functional components with named exports
- Use "function" keyword for components (not const)
- Minimize 'use client' - favor Server Components
- Use Suspense with fallback for client components
- Structure: exported component, subcomponents, helpers, types

**Naming Conventions:**
- Directories: lowercase with dashes (e.g., `auth-wizard`)
- Components: PascalCase files (e.g., `HeroSection.tsx`)
- Variables: camelCase with auxiliary verbs (e.g., `isLoading`, `hasError`)

**Styling:**
- Use Tailwind utilities exclusively - no inline styles
- Use semantic tokens: `bg-primary`, not `bg-[#3E5661]`
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Use Tailwind's opacity modifiers: `bg-primary/90` for hover
- Consistent spacing: multiples of 4 (e.g., `p-4`, `py-8`)

### Component Patterns

**Buttons:**
```tsx
// Primary action
<button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90">

// Secondary action
<button className="border-2 border-primary text-primary bg-transparent hover:bg-primary hover:text-primary-foreground">

// Critical CTA
<button className="bg-accent-deep-navy text-accent-deep-navy-foreground hover:bg-accent-deep-navy/90 text-lg font-bold px-8 py-4">

// Premium feature
<button className="bg-accent-golden text-accent-golden-foreground hover:bg-accent-golden/90 text-xl font-bold">
```

**Sections:**
```tsx
// Warm background section
<section className="bg-tertiary text-tertiary-foreground py-16">

// Standard card
<div className="bg-card text-card-foreground border border-border rounded-lg p-6">
```

**Text Hierarchy:**
```tsx
<p className="text-foreground">      {/* Primary text */}
<p className="text-muted-foreground"> {/* Secondary text */}
<p className="text-primary font-semibold"> {/* Emphasis */}
```

### Performance & Optimization

- Optimize images: WebP format, lazy loading
- Dynamic loading for non-critical components
- Minimize 'useEffect' and 'useState'
- Use React Server Components by default
- Implement proper loading states

### Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)

- All interactive elements must have focus states
- Use focus-visible:ring-2 for keyboard navigation
- Ensure 4.5:1 contrast for body text
- Ensure 3:1 contrast for UI components
- Never rely on color alone to convey meaning
- Provide text alternatives for icons

### Git & Deployment

**Commit Messages:**
- Format: `type(scope): description`
- Types: feat, fix, refactor, style, docs, test
- Example: `feat(colors): implement new brand palette`

**Deployment:**
- Main branch auto-deploys to production
- Test builds locally: `npm run build`
- Verify no TypeScript errors before pushing
- Check for console errors after deployment

**API Endpoints:**
- `/api/git-content` - File access (GET)
- `/api/git-content` - File updates (POST) - requires Bearer token
- `/api/health` - Health check

### Critical Constraints

**DO NOT:**
- Break the globals.css token mappings
- Use raw colors anywhere (hex, rgb, hsl)
- Remove existing shadcn/ui tokens
- Modify @theme inline structure carelessly
- Deploy without running build locally
- Use colors that fail accessibility (check guidelines)
- Modify imports in globals.css (@import, @plugin)

**ALWAYS:**
- Use semantic color tokens
- Test in both light and dark mode
- Verify accessibility contrast ratios
- Preserve backwards compatibility
- Run `npm run build` before committing
- Check console for CSS variable errors
- Reference component patterns above

### Brand Voice

Pattern Growth is the "Diagnostic Strategist":
- Insightful, calm, intellectually generous
- Trusted thinking partner who earns authority through precision
- "Your brand is not a megaphone — it's a flashlight"
- Focus on clarity, empathy, and synthesis over noise

### Common Issues & Solutions

**Issue:** Colors not appearing
- **Fix:** Check @theme inline mapping exists
- **Fix:** Verify token defined in both :root and .dark

**Issue:** Dark mode broken
- **Fix:** Ensure .dark class toggled on root element
- **Fix:** Verify dark mode color values adjusted (lighter, desaturated)

**Issue:** Accessibility failures
- **Fix:** Use provided accessible pairings
- **Fix:** Check contrast with WebAIM Contrast Checker

**Issue:** Build errors
- **Fix:** Verify no syntax errors in globals.css
- **Fix:** Ensure no undefined CSS variables

### Documentation

When making changes:
1. Update code comments for complex logic
2. Update README.md for new features
3. Document color usage in components
4. Maintain example patterns

### Response Style

- Be direct and technical
- Provide actual code, not high-level descriptions
- Suggest solutions proactively
- Anticipate edge cases
- Treat me as an expert but explain "why" for major decisions

### Testing Checklist

Before considering any change complete:
- [ ] Runs locally without errors
- [ ] Builds successfully (`npm run build`)
- [ ] Tested in light and dark mode
- [ ] No console errors
- [ ] Accessibility verified (contrast ratios)
- [ ] Responsive on mobile and desktop
- [ ] Git commit with clear message

---

**Remember:** This is a PRODUCTION site serving real users. Every change must maintain 100% functionality while improving the experience. When in doubt, preserve existing behavior and ask for clarification.

**Priority Order:**
1. Don't break anything (functionality preservation)
2. Maintain accessibility (WCAG compliance)
3. Follow token system (no raw colors)
4. Match designer specs (color accuracy)
5. Improve user experience (thoughtful enhancements)

